# CSS Conventions

All styles live in `css/styles.css`. Mobile-first — add complexity at breakpoints, never strip it away.

## Design tokens (use these, don't hardcode)
```css
--color-navy: #1e3a5f;
--color-gold: #c9a227;
--color-bg: #f8f7f4;
--header-height: 64px;
--sidebar-width: 240px;
--container-max: 1200px;
```

## Breakpoints
| Min width | Behavior |
|-----------|----------|
| 640px | 2-column product grid |
| 768px | Desktop nav, category sidebar (sticky), hide chips |
| 1024px | 3–4 column grids |

## Category sidebar (768px+)
Sidebar is sticky below the header:
```css
position: sticky;
top: calc(var(--header-height) + 1.25rem);
max-height: calc(100vh - var(--header-height) - 2.5rem);
overflow-y: auto;
```

## Icons
Style SVG icons via `.icon svg` — category icons use `renderCategoryIcon()` from JS, not emoji or icon fonts.

## Components
Reuse existing classes: `.btn`, `.btn-primary`, `.product-card`, `.category-card`, `.modal-overlay`, `.category-chip`.

## Accessibility
- Support `prefers-reduced-motion`
- Maintain 44px minimum tap targets on interactive elements
- Use `clamp()` for fluid heading sizes
